      "summaries": {
        "en": "Pi-mono is an AI agent toolkit that simplifies building and deploying intelligent assistants by providing unified interfaces across different platforms. Its technical innovation lies in offering consistent APIs for both terminal and web interfaces, allowing developers to create agents that work seamlessly in CLI, Slack, and web environments. You can use it to quickly prototype coding assistants, integrate LLMs into existing workflows, or deploy vLLM-powered pods for scalable inference, making it practical for both experimentation and production applications.",
        "zh": "Pi-mono是一个AI智能体工具包，旨在通过统一的多平台接口简化智能助手的构建与部署。其核心设计在于提供一致的API层，使开发者能够创建在命令行终端、Slack聊天界面和Web应用中无缝工作的智能体。该工具包包含编码助手CLI、TUI与Web UI库等组件，技术亮点是让同一套逻辑可适配不同交互场景。你可以用它快速原型化编程辅助工具，将大语言模型集成到现有工作流中，或部署基于vLLM的推理服务，非常适合需要跨平台智能体解决方案的实际项目。",
        "es": "Pi-mono is an AI agent toolkit that simplifies building and deploying intelligent assistants by providing unified interfaces across different platforms. Its technical innovation lies in offering consistent APIs for both terminal and web interfaces, allowing developers to create agents that work seamlessly in CLI, Slack, and web environments. You can use it to quickly prototype coding assistants, integrate LLMs into existing workflows, or deploy vLLM-powered pods for scalable inference, making it practical for both experimentation and production applications.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "pi-mono gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Pi-mono is an AI agent toolkit that simplifies building and deploying intelligent assistants by providing unified interfaces across different platforms. Its technical innovation lies in offering consistent APIs for both terminal and web interfaces, allowing developers to create agents that work seamlessly in CLI, Slack, and web environments. You can use it to quickly prototype coding assistants, integrate LLMs into existing workflows, or deploy vLLM-powered pods for scalable inference, making it practical for both experimentation and production applications.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
